.Dd November 13, 2026
.Dt NQDSYN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqdsyn
.Nd write a synthetic CSV file from its schema, marked synthetic
.Sh LIBRARY
libnqd, \-lnqd \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In nqd.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqdsyn
.Fa "nqdrec *r" "const char *dir" "const char *path" "uint64_t seed"
.Fa "uint64_t rows" "char *why" "size_t wcap"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqdsyn
writes a synthetic stand-in for the CSV file
.Fa path
to
.Fa dir Ns / Ns Fa path ,
made from the record's schema of
.Fa path
.Pq Xr noqtis-data 5 ,
its recipe, and records it in the
.Cm sources
of
.Fa r
with its SHA-256, size and
.Cm synthetic
true, so that every check of it says
.Ql [synthetic] .
Save the record with
.Xr nqdsave 3 .
It never replaces real data: a
.Fa path
whose source is not marked synthetic, or a file there that the record
does not mark synthetic, is refused.
.Pp
The file has the schema's delimiter, a header of the column names
unless
.Cm header
is false, and
.Fa rows
rows (0: the schema's
.Cm rows.min ,
else 100), each line ended by a line feed; a field that holds the
delimiter, a quote or a line break is quoted.
The values are the same for the same
.Fa seed
on every platform: they are drawn from the 64-bit big-endian words of
SHA-256("noqtis-syn-1" || 0x00 ||
.Fa seed
|| j), j = 0, 1, ..., each 8 bytes big-endian, four words a block, and
a whole number from 0 to
.Va k
\- 1 is a word
.Va x
taken when
.Va x
< 2^64 \- (2^64 mod
.Va k ) ,
as
.Va x
mod
.Va k
(a word not taken is skipped).
Row by row, column by column: when the column's
.Cm nulls
is true, a draw from 0 to 9 of 0 makes the value missing (the schema's
first
.Cm na
code, else empty); otherwise
.Bl -tag -width "text with a set"
.It Ql int
.Cm min
+ a draw from 0 to
.Cm max
\-
.Cm min
(defaults 0 and 1,000; at most 2^53 values)
.It Ql real
.Cm min
+
.Pf ( Cm max
\-
.Cm min )
\(mu
.Pf ( Va x
>> 11) / 2^53 (defaults 0 and 1), written as
.Xr nqdjson 3
writes numbers
.It Ql date
.Cm min
+ a draw of days to
.Cm max
(defaults 2000-01-01 and 2025-12-31)
.It Ql bool
.Ql true
for a draw from 0 to 1 of 1, else
.Ql false
.It Ql text No with a set
the element of
.Cm set
at a draw from 0 to its size \- 1
.It Ql text
eight letters
.Ql a
to
.Ql z ,
a draw from 0 to 25 each
.El
.Pp
Every value fits its column's type, range and set, so the file passes
the schema's columns; rules
.Pq Ql unique , Ql incr , No ...
are not part of the recipe.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Dv NQOK ,
or with a sentence in
.Fa why :
.Dv NQEARG
for no schema with columns,
.Fa path
not a capsule path, a source or file not marked synthetic, or an
.Ql int
range with no whole number or more than 2^53;
.Dv NQEIO
when the file cannot be written (its folder must exist);
.Dv NQELIM
over 1 GiB;
.Dv NQEMEM .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-data 1 ,
.Xr nqdinfer 3 ,
.Xr nqdnew 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-data 5
